*.pdf
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
api/
requirements.txt

# Internal docs, build scripts and Apps Script source. 93 of these were being served
# publicly at ifm-deploy.vercel.app (verified 200 on 7 Sep 2026) — build briefs, sheet
# IDs, sync scripts. Nothing the site renders fetches a .md/.py/.gs, so blocking them
# costs nothing. Add a "!" exception below if a page ever genuinely needs one.
*.md
*.py
*.gs
*.bak
*.orig
!3b-hero.mp4
!ifm-logo-gold-coins-spin.mp4

# Content-hub videos that MUST ship, or their catalogue rows 404 on the live site.
# The blanket *.mp4 above exists to keep ~778MB of raw footage out of the deploy;
# these are the small, already-compressed DERIVATIVES the hub actually links to.
# SIZE BUDGET (keep it, or this problem comes back): thumbs <=25KB, preview clips <=200KB.
# Masters (full-res photos, finished reels) belong on Drive, never here.
!content/teasers/*.mp4
!content/game-assets/*.mp4
!content/clips/*.mp4

# Saanp Seedhi test harness — puppeteer probes, a node_modules symlink and throwaway
# agent scripts. None of it is part of the game; shipping it would drag puppeteer into
# the deploy.
snakes-ladders/tests/

# HR, brand and tracker documents. Verified publicly readable on 7 Sep 2026 — including
# "Organization Chart/HR/3 - Sakshi Role Definition (internal).docx", a document about a
# named employee that says "internal" in its own filename. Nothing the site renders fetches
# a .docx/.xlsx/.csv (checked: zero references), so blocking them costs nothing.
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.env
*.key

# Sync-tool conflict copies ("... 2.html", "... 2.docx"). 650 of these appeared in the tree;
# 394 were not covered by the rules above and would each have become a live public URL.
* 2.*
*\ 2.*

# Scam Slingshot dev-only folders — MUST NOT SHIP.
# _reference holds real Angry Birds screenshots used privately as a critique baseline;
# publishing them would put Rovio's copyrighted art on the live site. _shots/_state/_tools
# are build scratch, capture harness and progress state — none of it belongs on the web.
scam-slingshot/_reference
scam-slingshot/_shots
scam-slingshot/_state
scam-slingshot/_tools
scam-slingshot/BUILDING-ELSEWHERE.md

# V1 Library prototype — ship only what the page needs. The rest is build tooling and
# review material that would otherwise each become a public URL.
content/v1-prototype/run-tests.js
content/v1-prototype/sample10.js
content/v1-prototype/tagged20.js
content/v1-prototype/storyboard.html
content/v1-prototype/enrichment.json
# Added 17 Sep 2026. Same reason as the five above, and the same trap: this list is
# per-file, so anything added to the prototype later is public by default until it is
# named here. The page loads taxonomy.js, v1-catalogue.js, media-map.js, transcripts.js
# and — since the §8 interpretation layer was wired in — interpreter.js, so that one is
# deliberately NOT listed below. The three that remain are test harness and internal
# audit material, carrying commentary and asset IDs never meant to be read off the
# open web.
content/v1-prototype/interpreter-tests.js
content/v1-prototype/nl-diagnostic.js
content/v1-prototype/semantic-experiment.js
# Dot-files are uploaded like any other file; this one is the HEAD-probe cache written by
# media-audit.py.
.media-probe.json
# The spec's reference pack. *.md above already blocks SPEC.md, but *.png is NOT blocked
# anywhere in this file, so without this line the approved storyboard and the current-state
# screenshots would each become a public URL on ifm-deploy. They are internal design
# material and nothing the site renders fetches them.
content/v1-prototype/references/
# The per-video transcript store written by transcribe-videos.py. 160 files, ~660KB, and
# nothing the page fetches: the text is already folded into v1-catalogue.js as each row's
# `speech` field. Publishing it would be 160 public URLs for no reader.
content/v1-prototype/speech/

# ── Deploy-size cuts, 22 Sep 2026. Vercel storage hit 100% of 10 GB. ──────────
# Each deploy shipped 427 MB; these three folders were 103 MB of it (24%) and
# NOTHING on the site loads any of them. Verified before removing, not assumed:

# Source archive for the Slash the Scam icons — 56 MB across 18 files at up to
# 5.6 MB each. Zero references to "game-icons/raw/" anywhere in the codebase.
# slash-the-scam.html loads the FLAT optimised set (game-icons/aidbox.png etc,
# 15 files totalling 1.9 MB), which stays shipped. raw/ is the working master.
game-icons/raw/

# 36.9 MB in TWO files (gold_war_crisis.png 29.9 MB, gold_low_rates.png 7 MB).
# Zero references. Wheel-of-Gold/Silver artwork that was never wired up.
game-icons/wog-wos-new/

# gstack QA tool output — browse-console.log, browse-network.log, qa-reports/.
# 10.5 MB, zero references, and it is debug output from the testing harness that
# should never have been web-accessible in the first place.
.gstack/
